@startuml
title Activiti 7 Guide-Documented Platform Examples - System Architecture
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam monochrome true

actor "Authenticated User" as AuthUser
actor "Task API User" as TaskUser
actor "Human Participant" as Human
actor "Cluster Operator" as Operator
actor "Developer / Integrator" as Dev

package "Identity and Security" {
  component "Keycloak\n(SSO / Token Issuer)" as Keycloak
  component "Spring Boot Application Context" as SpringBoot
  component "Spring Security\n(user, group, role, logged-in context)" as SpringSecurity
}

package "Activiti Cloud Runtime" {
  component "Gateway / API Gateway" as Gateway <<background>>
  component "Example Runtime Bundle" as RuntimeBundle
  component "ProcessRuntime API" as ProcessRuntime
  component "TaskRuntime API" as TaskRuntime
  component "Audit Service" as AuditService
  component "Query Service" as QueryService
  component "Notification Service" as NotificationService <<background>>
  component "Cloud Connectors" as CloudConnectors <<background>>
}

package "Kubernetes / GKE Deployment" {
  component "Kubernetes / GKE Cluster" as K8s
  component "NGINX Ingress Controller" as Ingress
  component "Public IP" as PublicIP
  component "Deployment Descriptors" as DeploymentDescriptors
  component "Kubernetes Registry / ConfigMaps" as Registry <<background>>
}

AuthUser --> Keycloak : obtain authentication token
AuthUser --> Gateway : protected user endpoint request\nwith valid token
Gateway --> RuntimeBundle : route authenticated requests
Gateway --> ProcessRuntime : route process requests
Gateway --> TaskRuntime : route task requests
Gateway --> AuditService : route audit requests
Gateway --> QueryService : route query requests

Keycloak --> SpringSecurity : token / identity integration
SpringBoot --> SpringSecurity : security context
SpringSecurity --> RuntimeBundle : authenticated context
SpringSecurity --> ProcessRuntime : authenticated context
SpringSecurity --> TaskRuntime : logged-in user +\nACTIVITI_USER / ROLE_ACTIVITI_USER

AuthUser --> ProcessRuntime : view process definitions\nstart SimpleProcess instance
ProcessRuntime --> RuntimeBundle : process definition lookup\nstart SimpleProcess
RuntimeBundle --> AuditService : audit events for\njust-started process instance
RuntimeBundle --> QueryService : process execution information
TaskUser --> TaskRuntime : task operations
TaskRuntime --> Human : human task participation
ProcessRuntime <--> TaskRuntime : combined documented full example

Operator --> Ingress : configure ingress
Operator --> PublicIP : configure public IP exposure
Ingress --> PublicIP : external access point
Ingress --> Gateway : route external requests
Ingress --> RuntimeBundle : route to selected internal services
K8s --> Gateway : hosts
K8s --> RuntimeBundle : hosts
K8s --> ProcessRuntime : hosts
K8s --> TaskRuntime : hosts
K8s --> AuditService : hosts
K8s --> QueryService : hosts
DeploymentDescriptors --> K8s : input rate + replica count parameters
Registry --> K8s : registry / config maps

Dev --> ProcessRuntime : follows example
Dev --> TaskRuntime : follows example
Dev --> RuntimeBundle : module reference

note right of Gateway
  Architecture background components:
  Gateway, Query Service, Notification Service,
  Cloud Connectors, Kubernetes registry/config maps.
  They remain background unless a functional requirement
  assigns explicit behavior.
end note

note bottom of RuntimeBundle
  Example Runtime Bundle hosts deployed
  process definitions, including SimpleProcess.
end note

note bottom of DeploymentDescriptors
  Scalability experiments: data input rate and
  cloud component replica counts are configurable.
end note

note bottom of SpringBoot
  Compatibility context:
  Activiti 7.0.0-EA-201802 aligned with
  Spring Boot 2.0.0.RELEASE and Spring Cloud Finchley.M8.
  Point-in-time context only.
end note

@enduml
